From: laurent at cbs.dtu.dk (Laurent Gautier)
Date: Wed, 01 Dec 2010 19:57:08 +0100
Subject: [BioC] org.*.eg.db problem
In-Reply-To: <487089.86735.qm@web86703.mail.ird.yahoo.com>
References: <487089.86735.qm@web86703.mail.ird.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <4CF69A84.8030501@cbs.dtu.dk>

Even shorter, one could use the "::" operator and write 
org.Mm.eg.db::egCHRLOC.

The presumed issue is more that one could import (attach) several 
org.X.eg.db packages, still write egCHRLOC and get something dependent 
on the order in which the import was made (hence the note about 
implementing the pattern "safely").

The only way around I can thing of would be to do not export names out a 
package namespace, forcing the use of ":::", but that's twisting things 
a little.



L.





